###Strategy

Since we can add terms in any order, let's rearrange the expression so like terms are next to each other.

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}10\blueE{k}+\goldE{1}+8\blueE{k}+\goldE{2}
\\\\
&=10\blueE{k}+8\blueE{k}+\goldE{1}+\goldE{2}
\end{align}$

Are there any like terms that we can combine?

[[☃ explanation 2]]

options.explanation:
$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\purpleD{x}+3\maroonD{y}+\goldE{7}+5\purpleD{x}-\goldE{2}
\\\\
&=1\purpleD{x}+5\purpleD{x}+3\maroonD{y}+\goldE{7}-\goldE{2}
\\\\
&=(1+5)\purpleD{x}+3\maroonD{y}+\goldE{7}-\goldE{2}
\\\\
&=6\purpleD{x}+3\maroonD{y}+\goldE5
\end{align}$

Notice that can combine $\purpleD{x}$ and $5\purpleD{x}$, but we cannot combine $6\purpleD{x}+3\maroonD{y}$ since they aren't like terms.

